#. Hint under the CNPJ field in the checkout dialogs, shown only to buyers in Brazil. CNPJ is the Brazilian company registration number, keep it as is. The Brazilian Consumer Defense Code is the Código de Defesa do Consumidor, and the right of withdrawal is the direito de arrependimento in its article 49. Use the usual name of that law in your language.
#: src/features/premium/components/BusinessPurchaseField.tsx
msgid "With a CNPJ, this is a business purchase, so the 7-day right of withdrawal in the Brazilian Consumer Defense Code doesn't apply to it, unless Brazilian law treats your company as a consumer."
msgstr "Ja norādīts CNPJ, tas ir uzņēmuma pirkums, tāpēc uz to neattiecas Brazīlijas Patērētāju tiesību aizsardzības kodeksa 7 dienu atteikuma tiesības, ja vien Brazīlijas tiesību akti tavu uzņēmumu neuzskata par patērētāju."

#. Line in the dialog for an Operator Pass someone passed on to you. The Operators' wall is the list of Operators on the homepage. Operator is the badge name and #operators is a channel name, keep both as is. {labsName} is the community name. Name these things plainly and never call them a bonus, a perk, free or included.
#: src/features/premium/utils/PremiumMessageDescriptors.ts
msgid "With a pass on your account, you have the Operator badge, a spot on the Operators' wall and #operators in {labsName}."
msgstr "Ja tavā kontā ir caurlaide, tev ir Operator nozīmīte, vieta Operatoru sienā un kanāls #operators kopienā {labsName}."

